Gizmo, a gnome warlock with a mischievous glint in his eye, stalked through the dense foliage of Stranglethorn Vale. His succubus, Lilith, slinked beside him, her crimson eyes scanning for danger. A group of trolls lumbered into view, their guttural chants echoing through the jungle. Gizmo grinned, a wicked plan forming. Lilith, with a seductive wink, ensnared the lead troll with Seduction, leaving him helpless and confused. Gizmo unleashed a barrage of shadowbolts, cackling with glee as the trolls fell one by one.

**Answer:** Voidwalkers are more popular because they are tankier and better at soloing difficult content, which is important for leveling in Classic WoW. While succubi offer utility, their lower survivability makes them less reliable for solo play. 


 [end of text]


